.SH NAME
.PP
getSchema \- get a reference to the specified Schema
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.getSchema(<name>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to get a reference to the specified Schema.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
name ( \f[I]string, required\f[] )
.PP
The name of the Schema.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
The common exceptions of \f[C]getSchema()\f[] function are as follows:
